From 351adf33517475bc8c9db9c14c0d7199049ca057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:14:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/92] deepseek4 : a large prefill ubatch's attention in query
 chunks (SiegeLadder P13, LLAMA_DSV4_ATTN_QCHUNK=nq, off by default)

With P11 the prompt ubatch is 4608-6144 tokens and attention became the prefill's main compute: every query ran
FlashAttention over the whole SWA ring of the ubatch (ub + 128 cells padded to 256 - 6400 at 6144, of which a query
needs 128) and over the compressed columns up to the ubatch's maximum (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.85: ~40 of 107 s of the
30K document at -ub 6144). Now each layer's attention runs in chunks of ~nq queries inside the same graph:
- per chunk its own window rows of the ring, gathered by cell index from the ring after this layer's write (the
  ring wraps; new input p13_rows, I32, the rows in position order padded with a masked real row) with their own
  continuous F16 mask (p13_mask, the rules of set_input_kq_mask), and the compressed columns only up to the chunk's
  own max n_visible padded to 256 (the top-k mask built at full width and sliced, never narrowed before set_rows);
- MoE and everything outside attention stays on the whole ubatch; each chunk's tail (Hadamard back, rope_back by
  its positions, wo_a) follows its FA call in graph order, chunks are joined pairwise, wo_b runs once; layers 0-1
  take the window slice only; P7 (LLAMA_DSV4_ATTN_SPLIT) is off while P13 is on;
- the per-chunk views of graph inputs (p13_mask, inp_hca's mask, inp_pos) are made once per graph (a view of an
  input per layer cost the scheduler a separate synchronous copy each); the reserve uses chunks of exactly nq, the
  worst case of every runtime chunk; one sequence, FA, causal SWA, raw cache f16 / q8_0 / q4_0, n_tokens >= 2 nq
  (LLAMA_DSV4_ATTN_QCHUNK_MIN), else the old path;
- LLAMA_DSV4_ATTN_QCHUNK_IDENTITY=1: one chunk with the ring in ring order and the full widths - K, mask and FA
  are those of the old path, bitwise.

Drafted by an agent from SiegeLadder docs/v41/p13-design.md, reviewed by a second one (two fixes applied: input
views once per graph, the reserve's worst case). SiegeLadder (bench/results/p2/p13): default path unchanged (n1p
text = trace, o32's counters); identity vs off on the 30K document at -ub 6144 KL 0.000000 over 128 answer
positions; nq 1536 - the document 107.4 -> 93.2 s (-13%), the consultant 276.3 / 279.0 -> 320.6 / 320.8 tok/s; not
bitwise (FA's tiles): KL 0.0041 on the first answer tokens (other prefill changes gave ~0.01, runs.md 4.85).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
